Configuración en disco
Ejecute el siguiente comando para comprobar las reglas en disco:
#!/usr/bin/env bash
{
for PARTITION in $(findmnt -n -l -k -it $(awk '/nodev/ { print $2 }'
/proc/filesystems | paste -sd,) | grep -Pv "noexec|nosuid" | awk '{print
$1}'); do
for PRIVILEGED in $(find "${PARTITION}" -xdev -perm /6000 -type f); do grep -qr "${PRIVILEGED}" /etc/audit/rules.d && printf "OK:
'${PRIVILEGED}' found in auditing rules.\n" || printf "Warning: '${PRIVILEGED}' not found in on disk configuration.\n"
done done
}
Genera el siguiente resultado OK.
Ejecutando configuración
Ejecute el siguiente comando para comprobar las reglas cargadas:
#!/usr/bin/env bash
{
RUNNING=$(auditctl -l)
[ -n "${RUNNING}" ] && for PARTITION in $(findmnt -n -l -k -it $(awk '/nodev/ { print $2 }' /proc/filesystems | paste -sd,) | grep -Pv "noexec|nosuid" | awk '{print $1}'); do
for PRIVILEGED in $(find "${PARTITION}" -xdev -perm /6000 -type f); do printf -- "${RUNNING}" | grep -q "${PRIVILEGED}" && printf "OK:
'${PRIVILEGED}' found in auditing rules.\n" || printf "Warning: '${PRIVILEGED}' not found in running configuration.\n"
done done \
|| printf "ERROR: Variable 'RUNNING' is unset.\n"
}
